# Android (TWA)
# The generated Gradle project is build output — `node scripts/build-twa.mjs`
# recreates it. twa-manifest.json is generated too, from the environment.
android-twa/

# The Play build, which is the same app with Play Billing linked. Its own
# directory because the two differ in their dependencies — see `android-gapp`.
android-twa-gapp/

# Signing keys, wherever they turn up. The Android key cannot be rotated out of
# a mistake — publishing it lets anybody ship an update as this app — so it is
# ignored by shape as well as by location, and `make lint` fails if one is ever
# tracked anyway. See scripts/check-no-secrets.mjs.
*.keystore
*.keystore.pass
*.jks
*.p12
*.pfx
# Signing keys never go in a repository. Play ties an app to its key forever:
# a leaked key lets someone else ship an update to your users, and a lost one
# means republishing under a new listing.
*.keystore
*.jks


# The signing key password lives beside the key; neither belongs in git.
*.keystore.pass
*.pass.*.bak

# ── Local only ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Machine-specific overrides and the files a working checkout accumulates that
# are not the product.
#
# Anything particular to ONE person's setup goes in `.git/info/exclude`
# instead, which is not part of the repository. That is the whole difference:
# this file is published, so every line in it describes something to whoever
# reads it — the editor somebody uses, the notes they keep, the container they
# work in. None of that is anybody else's business, and an ignore file is a
# strange place to announce it. `tests/ignore-files-say-nothing.test.ts` fails
# if anything named in .git/info/exclude turns up here.
#
# The leading slashes matter and are not tidiness: an unanchored pattern
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth — back when this repo was named
# `server/`, the bare pattern also swallowed `src/lib/server/`, and every new
# file added there stopped appearing in `git status`. Two of them were missing
# from the repository before anybody noticed.
/local.mk

# Coverage reports (yarn test:coverage)
coverage/

# Dropped-in asset bundles. `static/` is served to the public verbatim, so an
# archive left there is a 1.5MB download somebody can find — and it went into
# the history once, from a `git add -A`, before anybody noticed. The one copy
# of the logo is src/lib/logo/mark.png; a delivery it came in is not an asset.
/static/*.zip
/static/*.tar.gz

# And beside the logo itself: the vector it was delivered as, and the copies
# you keep of the one before it. `src/lib/logo/mark.png` is the single source
# every icon is generated from — the rest is your working material, and a
# `git add -A` swept it into the history once, along with an older mark that
# then became the source. Ignored so that cannot happen twice.
/src/lib/logo/mark.svg
/src/lib/logo/mark~*.png
/src/lib/logo/mark~*.svg

# Built packages, and the tree they are staged in.
dist/
.package-work/

# claude-docker local state (may contain credentials)
.claude-docker/
.claude-docker-EMERGENCY-BACKUP-*.tar.gz

# What `make fdroid` writes: the recipe and listing to paste into a fork of
# fdroiddata, and the two things a person has to post. Regenerated per release,
# never committed — the copy that matters lives in F-Droid's repository.
fdroid-out/

# Copied from node_modules by scripts/copy-sqlite-wasm.mjs on dev and build.
/static/sqlite3.wasm
.worktrees/
build-isolated/
capacitor/node_modules/

# Each flavour's suggested instance, written at build time. The DEV app's is
# this machine's address on the wifi, which is nobody else's; a build that has
# none falls back to the official instance, which is what a store build wants
# anyway.
capacitor/android/app/src/*/assets/public/
scripts/demo-media/birds/

